        <div class="lab-intro"><p><strong>Your matrix, your missing entries, your assumptions.</strong> Follow the process from the GIRO presentation, pages 3–7. Matrices are ordinary Pearson correlations; partial correlations use a dot.</p><span id="connection-state">Local Python package</span></div>
        <div class="workspace general-workspace">
          <aside class="controls general-controls">
            <div class="control-heading"><h3>Build your experiment</h3><button id="reset-lab" class="reset">Reset example ↺</button></div>
            <label for="source">Start with</label><select id="source"><option value="preset">Notebook worked example</option><option value="generated">Generate a valid matrix</option><option value="manual">Enter a matrix manually</option><option value="three">Three-variable example</option></select>
            <div id="generation" hidden><label for="dimension">Number of variables</label><select id="dimension"><option>3</option><option>4</option><option selected>5</option><option>6</option><option>7</option></select><label for="seed">Generation seed</label><input id="seed" type="number" min="0" max="4294967295" value="42" step="1"><button id="generate" class="lab-button">Generate full matrix</button><small>R = D⁻¹(AAᵀ + 0.5I)D⁻¹. The seed reproduces the same positive definite input.</small></div>
            <div id="manual" hidden><label for="matrix-json">Paste a symmetric correlation matrix</label><textarea id="matrix-json" rows="6" spellcheck="false" placeholder="[[1,0.5,null],[0.5,1,0.5],[null,0.5,1]]"></textarea><button id="apply-matrix" class="lab-button">Use this matrix</button><small>3–7 variables, unit diagonal, symmetric entries. Use null or ? for missing pairs. Asymmetric input is rejected.</small></div>
            <div class="control-divider"></div><label for="mask-count">Hide additional known pairs</label><div class="two-inputs"><input id="mask-count" aria-label="Number of pairs to hide" type="number" min="0" step="1" value="3"><input id="mask-seed" aria-label="Mask seed" title="Mask seed" type="number" min="0" value="7" step="1"></div><small>Pair count / mask seed. Random masking can create a nonchordal pattern.</small><button id="random-mask" class="lab-button secondary">Hide pairs randomly</button><button id="restore-input" class="plain-button">Restore initial entries</button>
            <div class="control-divider"></div><label for="method">Completion objective</label><select id="method"><option value="max_entropy">Maximum determinant (chordal)</option><option value="vine">Explicit vine partial correlations</option></select><small id="method-note">For chordal inputs. The optimum is independent of the displayed vine representation.</small><label for="strategy">Vine structure</label><select id="strategy"><option value="greedy">Greedy: prioritise known / strong edges</option><option value="c-vine">C-vine: ordered roots</option><option value="d-vine">D-vine: ordered path</option></select><label for="order">Variable order</label><input id="order" value="1,2,3,4,5" aria-describedby="order-note"><small id="order-note">A permutation of the labels. Used by C- and D-vines; greedy chooses its own edges.</small>
            <button id="complete" class="lab-button primary">Complete this matrix →</button><p class="local-compute">Computed by the existing Python package on this computer. Only the incomplete matrix and chosen assumptions are sent to the local solver.</p>
          </aside>
          <div class="results general-results">
            <div class="result-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow" id="dataset-label">Notebook worked example</span><h3 id="stage-title">Prepare the incomplete matrix</h3></div><span class="status" id="lab-status" role="status">Preparing…</span></div>
            <nav class="process-steps" aria-label="Completion process"><button data-step="0" class="active"><span>1</span> Input & graph</button><button data-step="1"><span>2</span> Expand vine</button><button data-step="2"><span>3</span> Assign partials</button><button data-step="3"><span>4</span> Reconstruct</button><button data-step="4"><span>5</span> Result & compare</button></nav>
            <div id="lab-error" class="lab-error" role="alert" hidden></div><div id="input-feedback" class="input-feedback" aria-live="polite"></div>
            <section class="stage" id="stage-0">
              <p class="stage-intro">Choose the information available to the solver. Known entries become graph edges, including a known zero. Missing entries remain unknown.</p>
              <div class="editor-toolbar"><div class="segmented"><button id="mask-mode" class="selected" aria-pressed="true">Click to hide / restore</button><button id="edit-mode" aria-pressed="false">Click to edit a value</button></div><span id="pair-count"></span></div>
              <div class="input-visuals"><div><div id="editable-matrix"></div><p class="cell-detail">Click an off-diagonal entry. Changes apply symmetrically; the diagonal stays at one.</p><div class="pair-editor" id="pair-editor" hidden><label for="pair-value" id="pair-label">Correlation</label><input id="pair-value" type="number" step="0.05" min="-0.999999" max="0.999999"><button id="set-pair">Set known value</button><button id="hide-pair">Mark missing</button></div></div><div class="input-network"><h4>Observed graph</h4><div id="observed-graph"></div><p>Weights are supplied correlations. Absence of an edge means unavailable information.</p></div></div>
              <div class="stage-actions"><span>The solver cannot see hidden reference values.</span><button data-next="1">Inspect the vine →</button></div>
            </section>
            <section class="stage" id="stage-1" hidden><p class="stage-intro">Each node in the next tree represents an edge of the preceding tree. Eligible edges obey the proximity condition. Labels below are derived from the actual variable sets.</p><p id="vine-policy" class="process-note"></p><div class="tree-gallery" id="vine-trees"></div><div class="stage-actions"><span>Orange ? indicates a free partial correlation.</span><button data-next="2">Choose the partials →</button></div></section>
            <section class="stage" id="stage-2" hidden><p id="assignment-explanation" class="stage-intro"></p><div id="assignments"></div><div class="process-note">Partial correlation describes linear regression residuals. It is not generally conditional correlation and does not select a copula family. A free first-tree edge has no conditioning variables, so it is an ordinary correlation.</div><div class="stage-actions"><span id="assignment-summary"></span><button id="complete-from-partials">Run completion →</button></div></section>
            <section class="stage" id="stage-3" hidden><p class="stage-intro" id="reconstruction-note">Run completion to inspect the numerical steps for this matrix and policy.</p><div class="trace-toolbar"><button id="trace-prev" aria-label="Previous reconstruction step">←</button><span id="trace-position">No trace yet</span><button id="trace-next" aria-label="Next reconstruction step">→</button></div><div id="trace-content"></div><div class="stage-actions"><span>Intermediate calculations are not final validation.</span><button data-next="4">Inspect the result →</button></div></section>
            <section class="stage" id="stage-4" hidden><div id="general-result"><p class="stage-intro">Complete the current input to see a result. Changing an input or strategy clears the previous result and certificate.</p></div><div id="ground-truth" hidden><button id="reveal-truth" class="lab-button secondary">Reveal hidden reference & compare</button><div id="truth-content" hidden></div></div><div class="stage-actions"><span id="result-provenance">Checks are recomputed for the current input.</span><button id="export-general" disabled>Download scenario ↓</button></div></section>
            <p class="result-limit">Illustrative inputs. No empirical insurance calibration or tail-dependence validation. Positive definite specified cliques are necessary, but do not prove general nonchordal feasibility. No silent strategy substitution is made.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
